content:
Analyzing the datasheet: ordering defines two SKUs (C-temp and I-temp); protocols list 1000Base-LXD and 1G FC with industry-standard rates (1.25 Gbps GbE, 1.0625 Gbps FC). Receiver footnote ties specs to 1.25 Gbps. No row links `100Base-LXD` to a pool bit rate — omitting it. Treating `SO-SFP-1000BASE-LXD` and `SO-SFP-1000Base-LXD` as one C-temp SKU per ordering table.

```json
{
  "modes": [
    {
      "label": "1000Base-LXD GbE C-temp",
      "model": "SO-SFP-1000Base-LXD",
      "standards_code": "1000Base-LXD",
      "bit_rate_gbps": 1.25
    },
    {
      "label": "1G FC C-temp",
      "model": "SO-SFP-1000Base-LXD",
      "standards_code": "1G FC",
      "bit_rate_gbps": 1.0625
    },
    {
      "label": "1000Base-LXD GbE I-temp",
      "model": "SO-SFP-1000Base-LXD-I",
      "standards_code": "1000Base-LXD",
      "bit_rate_gbps": 1.25
    },
    {
      "label": "1G FC I-temp",
      "model": "SO-SFP-1000Base-LXD-I",
      "standards_code": "1G FC",
      "bit_rate_gbps": 1.0625
    }
  ]
}
```
